      "suggested_fix": "Report relevance and date agreement for the initial and final prompts on the validation set, state that the validation set was used for prompt development, and validate the final prompt on fresh articles (the random sample proposed in Section 8)."
    },
    {
      "id": "ROB-004",
      "category": "missing_robustness_support",
      "finding_summary": "The headline full-run counts (92 relevant articles, 43 projects) depend on a prompt whose relevance definition was broadened. The authors say the pilot could not reveal the effect of that change, and no sensitivity check of the full-run counts to prompt version, reasoning level or model is reported.",
      "issue_type": "manuscript_issue",
      "severity": "medium",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "location": {
        "page": 6,
        "page_label": "6",
        "section": "3.2 LLM pipeline",
        "text_quote": "this change did not make a difference",
        "precision": "exact"
      },
      "claim_text": "Applied to 3,187 articles, the pipeline finds 92 articles reporting an opening, which we group into 43 projects across 14 of 15 counties.",
      "assessment": "partially",
      "cannot_verify_reason": null,
      "evidence_summary": "Section 3.2 says the prompt was altered to treat a wider selection of bicycle infrastructure as relevant. The authors state this 'did not make a difference' in the pilot only because the pilot analysed only sykkelvei articles. The pilot therefore cannot show how the change affects the full run. The paper does not state whether the 3,187 articles are also restricted to this search term. Settings with possible influence (reasoning level 'low', default temperature, a single model chosen for cost) are not varied. Section 8 acknowledges that a random sample of the full run should be checked against human coding, but the abstract and conclusion give the counts without qualification.",
      "source_objects": [
        {
          "id": "S1",
          "type": "text",
          "label": "Prompt broadening",
