          "path": "work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_012.md",
          "page": 12,
          "page_label": "12",
          "section": "8 Next Steps",
          "text_quote": "a random sample from the full run of 3,187 articles should also be checked against",
          "url": null,
          "object_id": "OBJ-a6c6d31e7be45f25b775aa47",
          "correspondence": "text",
          "verification_note": null
        }
      ],
      "claim_evidence_links": [
        {
          "claim_text": "Full-run counts of 92 articles and 43 projects",
          "source_object_ids": [
            "S1",
            "S2",
            "S3"
          ],
          "relation": "partial",
          "note": "The counts come from a prompt version not tested in the pilot for the broadened relevance rule, with no sensitivity analysis; the paper itself flags a full-run check as future work."
        }
      ],
      "numeric_check": null,
      "suggested_fix": "State whether the full run used the same search term as the pilot. Report how many articles are classified relevant under the original and final prompts, or on a hand-checked random subsample of the full run. Qualify the counts in the abstract and conclusion as unvalidated until then."
    },
    {
      "id": "ROB-005",
      "category": "robustness_overstatement",
      "finding_summary": "The 'sufficiently high' internal consistency of the LLM rests on 3 repeated runs over 34 articles (1 disagreement) and covers relevance only. The consistency of the extracted opening date across runs is not reported, and few positives are involved.",
      "issue_type": "manuscript_issue",
      "severity": "low",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "location": {
        "page": 6,
        "page_label": "6",
        "section": "3.2 LLM pipeline",
        "text_quote": "only one (3%) showed disagreement between coding runs",
        "precision": "exact"
      },
      "claim_text": "Out of 34 articles, only one (3%) showed disagreement between coding runs. This was deemed a sufficiently high level of internal consistency for this paper.",
      "assessment": "partially",
      "cannot_verify_reason": null,
      "evidence_summary": "The consistency test was applied to 'the first-stage coding (relevant vs. not relevant)' only. Section 4.2 says the pilot coder and LLM agree on the date of all three relevant articles, based on the majority of three runs, and notes only that one run coded the Stord article as not relevant. No run-level date consistency is reported. With about 3–4 positive articles, 33 of 34 stable articles are mostly clear negatives, so the test says little about stability on relevant or borderline articles. The only unstable article is the borderline one. Run-to-run stability under the stated settings (reasoning 'low', default temperature) is therefore only weakly established.",
      "source_objects": [
        {
          "id": "S1",
          "type": "text",
          "label": "Internal consistency",
          "path": "work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_006.md",
