          "page_label": "6",
          "section": "3.2",
          "text_quote": "only one (3%) showed disagreement between coding runs",
          "url": null,
          "object_id": "OBJ-e13eccc23f4c883050d15bcf",
          "correspondence": "text",
          "verification_note": null
        },
        {
          "id": "S2",
          "type": "text",
          "label": "Majority-of-three-runs note",
          "path": "work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_008.md",
          "page": 8,
          "page_label": "8",
          "section": "4.2",
          "text_quote": "We note that one of the three LLM runs coded this article as not relevant.",
          "url": null,
          "object_id": "OBJ-b41cc221a4f064e5990acabf",
          "correspondence": "text",
          "verification_note": null
        }
      ],
      "claim_evidence_links": [
        {
          "claim_text": "Internal consistency is sufficiently high",
          "source_object_ids": [
            "S1",
            "S2"
          ],
          "relation": "partial",
          "note": "Relevance only, 34 articles, mostly negatives; date stability across runs not reported."
        }
      ],
      "numeric_check": null,
      "suggested_fix": "Report run-to-run agreement for opening date and precision on the relevant articles. State that the consistency statistic is for relevance only and rests on very few positive articles."
    },
    {
      "id": "ROB-006",
      "category": "missing_robustness_support",
      "finding_summary": "The statement that 'openings cluster before winter and summer holidays' is based on a ranking of monthly shares of relevant articles for which no figures, counts or table are reported. The authors note that July–August 2026 coverage is thin, and the measure is article publication timing, not opening date.",
      "issue_type": "manuscript_issue",
      "severity": "medium",
      "confidence": "high",
      "location": {
        "page": 10,
        "page_label": "10",
        "section": "5 Results",
        "text_quote": "This indicates that openings cluster before winter and summer holidays",
        "precision": "exact"
      },
      "claim_text": "October–December 2025 and May–June 2026 have the highest share of relevant articles, and February–April 2026 the lowest. This indicates that openings cluster before winter and summer holidays.",
      "assessment": "no",
      "cannot_verify_reason": null,
      "evidence_summary": "Table 6 and the surrounding text give totals only (3,187 articles; 92 relevant; 43 projects). No monthly shares or counts are shown, and no figure displays them. The claim therefore cannot be checked. The text concedes that 'the archive extraction contains few articles from July–August 2026'. Only 29 of 43 projects are dated to the day or month (Table 6: Year 9, Not stated 5), and the 'relevant' article share is based on article publication date. Moving from the share of relevant articles by month to a conclusion about when openings occur needs the opening dates, not publication dates. The sample spans one year (October 2025 to October 2026), so a seasonal pattern also cannot be separated from a one-off pattern.",
      "source_objects": [
        {
          "id": "S1",
          "type": "text",
          "label": "Seasonality statement",
          "path": "work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_010.md",
          "page": 10,
          "page_label": "10",
          "section": "5 Results",
          "text_quote": "This indicates that openings cluster before winter and summer holidays",
          "url": null,
          "object_id": "OBJ-e9b90e0f75ce05ff1ce150cc",
          "correspondence": "text",
          "verification_note": "Table 6 on the same page was read from page text, not from the structured table file."
        }
      ],
      "claim_evidence_links": [
        {
          "claim_text": "Openings cluster before winter and summer holidays",
          "source_object_ids": [
            "S1"
          ],
          "relation": "cannot_verify",
          "note": "No monthly counts or shares are shown; the caveat on July–August coverage is stated by the authors."
        }
      ],
      "numeric_check": null,
      "suggested_fix": "Report monthly numbers of articles and relevant articles (and, for dated projects, opening-month counts). Otherwise soften 'indicates' to a tentative observation, and distinguish publication timing from opening timing."
    },
